&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward Deployed AI Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global AI Strategy &amp;amp; Solutions defines how DEPT®’s clients respond as AI agents become the primary layer between customers and brands. The Future of the Customer Journey (FCJ) is the team’s flagship offer: it maps how AI systems intermediate customer journeys, diagnoses where a brand’s product reality diverges from what AI systems say about it, and directs investment accordingly. Growth and strategy teams across markets are selling and delivering it now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;Forward Deployed AI Engineer, you are an embedded builder inside that motion. You will sit with growth and strategy teams, understand the problem in front of them, and answer with working software rather than documentation. You will convert FCJ methodology into agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools, and integrate with infrastructure that lets new prototypes appear in days. When needed, you will work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, making sure the firm-wide strategy is captured and implemented properly rather than reinvented market by market. As components mature, you will collaborate with product and craft teams to keep everything compatible with the long-term platform and hand over cleanly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be given broad problem statements to help collaborate and solve, not specific product ideas and features to create. We are not looking for someone to lead on devops or CI/CD, this is about having great ideas that are sensitive to our clients’ real challenges, and shipping prototypes and strategic tools rapidly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your most important collaboration is with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy: deciding what gets built next, for which market, to unlock which engagement. The toolchain will keep changing underneath you, new models, new vendor products, new technology-partner platforms, and that is the point. This role suits an engineer who learns by shipping and treats every new AI product as something to master in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy, converting methodology into working agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with growth and strategy teams to understand their problems and provide working solutions at prototype pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, ensuring the firm-wide FCJ strategy is captured and implemented consistently across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and craft teams where necessary to document integration paths, maintain platform compatibility, and hand over validated components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technology partners to evaluate, adopt, and integrate new AI products; maintain an AI-native toolchain and share what works across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience prototyping and shipping software in any modern backend language (Python, TypeScript, Go, or similar), with the ability to leverage AI tooling to spin up prototype frontends and APIs quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building applications across the mainstream LLM model families (Gemini, GPT, Claude), connecting models to enterprise data and tools using patterns such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and skills-based agent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in working with APIs to connect different services, authentication, data exchange, and integration across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing agentic systems with orchestration frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native way of working: AI tooling is the default across coding, research, and delivery, with comfort spanning the tools in use across different markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a forward-deployed, customer engineering, solutions engineering, or applied AI role within an agency, consultancy, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting working software to non-technical stakeholders, including strategists and clients, and iterating live on their feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of emerging integration standards such as OpenAPI and Model Context Protocol (MCP) for connecting agents to business systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of any of the following: paid media, social platforms, user behaviour, agentic commerce, or generative engine optimisation (GEO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with evaluation, tracing, and observability for LLM applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated learning mindset: a record of adopting new AI products from technology partners quickly, learning by doing rather than waiting for training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible, hybrid working policy (2 days from the office in London).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent salary based on experience and equal pay policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension, free private healthcare, mental health support, and company sick pay scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days paid holiday (plus UK Bank Holidays).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help getting you to work with a season ticket loan and cycle to work scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family friendly policies to support new parents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social and Cultural Events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational Talks, bringing the outside in with regular guest speakers and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development, supporting your growth with continuous opportunities to learn and advance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buddy Programme: You will be paired with a ‘Buddy’ to help you through your first weeks’ at DEPT®.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/en-gb/insight/dept-is-a-certified-b-corporation/&quot;&gt;B Corp® since 2021&lt;/a&gt; and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global annual &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/&quot;&gt;DEPT® Cares Month&lt;/a&gt; in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hi 👋 we’re Genio. We create beautifully simple learning tools that boost knowledge, skills, and confidence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re a SaaS scale up and one of the fastest growing tech companies in the North.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There’s 90+ of us around the UK with our HQ in Leeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our software is award-winning and used by 100,000s of students at over 1,000 universities &amp;amp; colleges worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re growing so we can achieve our mission to support 1 million students to become better learners by 2030.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚀 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career track:&lt;/strong&gt; IC4&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Shared services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Platform Engineer, you help set the strategy for Genio&#39;s infrastructure end-to-end — from design through to running it in production. You work with squads on feature work to advise/set direction, and ensure reliability, security, and cost efficiency. You drive the design and implementation of best-practice cloud infrastructure, automation frameworks, and tooling that enable scalability, reliability, and efficiency for engineering teams in both business units. Working closely with engineers, testers, and data colleagues, you lead initiatives to enhance platform capabilities, optimise performance, and champion DevOps principles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolving Genio&#39;s cloud infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and optimise cloud infrastructure to ensure scalability, security, and resilience. Shape long-term infrastructure strategy and apply Infrastructure as Code and CI/CD best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintaining and improving observability of Genio&#39;s applications:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement comprehensive monitoring, alerting, and distributed tracing capabilities. Champion the adoption of SLOs, SLAs, and SLIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leading incidents and post-incident learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Support as an incident lead for PlatformOps, coordinate the response, run blameless post-incident reviews, and track actions to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving automation of repetitive tasks:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop scalable automation frameworks to streamline engineering workflows and improve efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raising the technical capability of other teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a technical advisor, provide guidance and upskilling support for platform tooling, and mentor engineers across engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👥 Meet the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the &lt;strong&gt;Principal Platform Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; and work most closely with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Principal Platform Engineer (Operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform Engineer (Operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering teams in both business units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Support Engineer (Operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior Data Engineer (Operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👤About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems design and judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; Takes an ambiguous problem, defines options, makes trade-offs explicit, and writes clear design documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong experience in scripting and programming with Python and/or Bash for automation and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure as Code:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficient with Terraform for infrastructure automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong experience with AWS or Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes in production:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience operating, upgrading, networking, and debugging Kubernetes clusters under load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability Engineering &amp;amp; Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ownership of production service reliability (defining SLIs, incident response) and implementing security practices (access control, secrets management, patching, backup/recovery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus / Nice to have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Assisted Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable and proficient with AI development tools as part of everyday engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cost Awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of infrastructure costs and the ability to build cases for spending changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to mentor others, foster trust, make pragmatic technology choices, and communicate with &quot;passionate views, loosely held&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💰Salary and benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸£70,000- £76,000 per annum dependent on experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖️ 33 days annual leave (Inclusive of bank holidays)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎄 3 gifted days off at Christmas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 EMI Share Options Scheme&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎓 Generous individual learning and training allowance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⌚ Truly flexible hours to suit when you work best&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻 Full home working set up and beautiful collaborative office space&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗 Free Leeds City Centre office parking&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Nomad working policy with family travel insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 Enhanced 26 weeks maternity and 4 weeks paternity (fully paid)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤍 Health cash plan (from glasses to massages)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸 6% employer pension contribution&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📍Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our beautiful office space in Leeds is our key hub for collaboration, and we love to get together in person. We operate a flexible hybrid working model, including supporting our Genios who are based remotely across the UK. If you are more than 50 miles away from the office, we offer full remote working support within the UK, with the opportunity to join colleagues for in-person collaboration several times a year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will discuss ways of working with you at interview however if you have any questions before you apply please reach out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 What to expect next:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll review your application and provide a response within 1 week. Even if it’s not the news you’d hoped for, we appreciate it’s good to know either way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If we invite you to meet with us for interview, here’s an overview of what the process will look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening interview with our Recruitment Business Partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A take-home technical test for you to complete offline and submit back to us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical interview with Mark, Staff Platform Engineer and an Engineer from the Platform Operations team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A CV review and Cultural &amp;amp; Values interview with Mark and our Head of Engineering, Mala&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ahead of your interview you will receive a confirmation email outlining who you’ll be meeting and when, anything you’ll need to prepare in advance and any resources we think you might find helpful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
